    ds_did_well: "the D6/R10 treatment is exactly right and stated as an AXIOM: 'an LLM never sits inside a latency- or safety-critical signal path' — the algedonic classifier is a deterministic decision tree, the LLM only produces proposals, digests and audit. The pre-registered experiment block refuses post-hoc reinterpretation and maps every hypothesis failure to a diagnosis in advance",
    findings: [
      "FORM, ¬content — and it is a finding about the RUBRIC. The document had been reflowed 907 → 1459 lines to reach w/l ≤ 5.0 and arrived with 91 lines of ≤2 words, plus FIVE `// ─── N. TITLE ───` headers split MID-PHRASE across two lines. Rejoined to 1303 lines at 4.53 w/l — STILL inside target, which proves the splitting bought nothing. The metric was satisfied and the document was harder to read than before: w/l falls when you break a sentence, so the target is gameable by splitting",
      "D6' ×2 — an ASCII apostrophe reading as a prime. ONE of them was a real document-local REFINEMENT of the canonical D6 (reflex/fast/safety deterministic vs deliberative tactical LLM-permitted). A mechanical sweep replaced it with a bare D6, which would have REDEFINED a canon rule inside a compliance table — caught on re-read, renamed D6.tactical using the suffix pattern the rubric declares for canon extensions (A8.vOS). The recertification clause working on me, ¬on DS",
      "the last explicit path in the corpus — /root/nucleus-wrapper.sh → @nucleus_wrapper. system/ now carries ZERO"],
    debt: "S4-GOLIVE-UNSIGNED — the whole anticipatory arc is BUILT, tested and DISCONNECTED. The flip is one env line; what is missing is the S5 signature, ¬the engineering. Behind it sits PHI-UP-PIPELINE: flipping before the kernel reads the projection would put a production flag on a loop with ∄ input",
    tool_notes: ["orphan-line share added to --density and deliberately left ADVISORY: gating it at 4% immediately flagged boot/ — hard_rules 9%, regulation_layer 8% — the CALIBRATION BASELINE. A dense notation line carries few lowercase words BY DESIGN, and '≤2 words' cannot separate that from a broken fragment without knowing whether the line CONTINUES the one above. Tuning the threshold until the baseline passes would be fitting the number, ¬the rule",
                  "--dupes still reports D6 as 'defined' in both S4 documents. Both are CORRECT: one is a verdict inside a block labelled compliance:, the other a mid-sentence citation at the start of a WRAPPED line. The definition/citation rule is positional and position cannot tell a definition from a continuation. Recorded as a known limit rather than 'fixed' by editing correct documents to satisfy the index"] },
  verify:      { parser: "VALID", paths: "0 in the whole corpus", density: "0 of 31 over target" },
}

