    ds_did_well: "the §4 DECISION PKI finding is the best security work in the corpus — DS read the verifier, found that it takes its verification key from the record it is verifying, contrasted it against beacon which does it right, and specified the fix as 'reach beacon's standard' rather than inventing one, with beacon's own 7-test discipline. It also states the exposure honestly: DEPLOYED, ¬yet actuating, and that margin is the whole reason it is not an incident",
    findings: [
      "§4's CRITICAL had ∄ debt marker. verify_decision() takes its key from a field IN THE RECORD: an attacker signs with their own key, embeds their own pubkey, and the record verifies VALID with ∄ cert-chain check. It runs deployed inside the audit logger ⟹ every `verified: true` in the trail currently means 'checked out against a key the signer chose'. Declared as DECISION-PKI-TRUSTS-RECORD, gate=blocks_B3 — wiring supervision_layer B3 before it passes turns a corrupt audit trail into a CONTROL INPUT",
      "§3 named netdata as the tier-2 signal source. rmw3 (S5) decommissioned netdata the same day — executed ∧ verified. Repointed at /proc/pressure/*, which hardware_ingest.rs already reads: ∄ daemon, ∄ API, ∄ port. Strictly better than what it replaces",
      "§11 listed FIVE open questions about killing S1s under host emergency, and the document ANSWERS the first in its own §1: '∀ grant: single-loop (A5) — resize ONLY, NO start/stop/create/destroy'. Stopping an S1 is outside S3's authority by the document's own axiom ⟹ CRITICAL kill is DOUBLE-LOOP, human. Open at §11, closed at §1, thirty lines up. The genuinely open rest — grace window, RATIFIED priority order, host-emergency scope beyond S1, tier-skipping — is S5 policy: debt(S3-EMERGENCY-KILL-POLICY)"],
    evidence_kept: "the live case that makes the policy question sharp: 112 (clima) was simultaneously the largest CPU consumer AND the one worth keeping. Consumption ≠ expendability ⟹ any automatic rule keyed on consumption gets it exactly backwards" },
  verify:      { parser: "VALID", d7: 0, density: "0 over target", debts: 35 },
}

